This repository contains the source code and analytical scripts required to reproduce the data processing, 
statistical analysis, and validation procedures presented in the manuscript. The repository is organized into 
three main directories: Data preprocessing, Data analysis, and Validation.

1. Data Preprocessing (/Data preprocessing)
This directory contains Python scripts used to clean and standardize the raw spatial datasets before core analyses.

CDR_to_Flow_Dakar.py: Converts raw Call Detail Records (CDRs) into origin-destination flow data.
Note: This script is exclusively applied to the Dakar dataset. Raw datasets for the other case cities were already obtained in a flow format.

Irregular_to_Gridded_Transformation.py: Transforms spatial data from irregular administrative or census units into a standardized gridded format 
to ensure consistent spatial resolution.
Note: This script is specifically applied to non-Chinese case cities. For details, please refer to the Materials and Methods section in the main text.

2. Data Analysis (/Data analysis)
This directory contains the core analytical scripts used to measure and model the spatial scaling behavior. It is divided into two sub-modules:

2.1 Scaling Measurement (/Scaling measurement)
Contains scripts to aggregate and quantify the spatial scaling characteristics of mobility flows and population distributions across varying spatial scales. 
These measurements serve as the empirical foundation for the subsequent parameterization.

2.2 Scaling Analysis (/Scaling analysis)
Contains MATLAB scripts that perform statistical estimations based on the measured scaling features:

Flow_scaling_regimes_identification.m: Identifies distinct flow scaling regimes and estimates the corresponding scaling parameters.

Population_scaling_analysis.m: Calculates the scaling parameters for spatial population distributions.

Flow_population_allometric_scaling_analysis.m: Computes the parameters governing the allometric scaling relationship between mobility flows and population.

3. Validation (/Validation)
This directory contains rigorous statistical tests and simulations designed to verify the robustness of the empirical findings and theoretical models.

Permutation test for trade-offs/: Conducts permutation tests to validate the observed systemic trade-offs against potential parameterization artifacts.
For theoretical background and detailed mathematical proofs, please refer to Supplementary Text S3.

Model_based_counterfactual_simulation/: Contains scripts to conduct counterfactual simulations that validate the efficacy of the analytical derivative and 
demonstrate the superior efficiency of the targeted spatial intervention strategy over global or random approaches.
For comprehensive simulation setups and derivations, please refer to Supplementary Texts S5 to S8.
